"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[68589],{68589:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n## Check Trading Holidays using exchange_calendars in python\\nWhen dealing with automated stock trading systems or financial data, checking whether the <mark>market is open</mark> is very important.  \\n`exchange_calendars` library allows you to easily manage the holidays of major exchanges worldwide, including the Korea Exchange (KRX).\\n### 1. Install Library\\nFirst, you need to install the necessary libraries.\\n```bash\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Install command\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ pip install exchange_calendars\\n```\\n### 2. Check KRX Trading Holiday\\nThis is code to retrieve the calendar for the Korea Exchange (XKRX) and check if today is a `session` (business day).\\n```python\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Trading Holiday Check Script\\"\\n}\\n---\\nimport datetime\\nimport exchange_calendars as xcals\\n\\ndef check_trading_day():\\n    try:\\n        # Create KRX calendar instance\\n        xkrx = xcals.get_calendar(\\"XKRX\\")\\n        \\n        # Check today\'s date (YYYY-MM-DD)\\n        today_str = datetime.datetime.today().strftime(\\"%Y-%m-%d\\")\\n        \\n        # Check if the market is open today\\n        if not xkrx.is_session(today_str):\\n            print(f\\"Today ({today_str}) is a trading holiday. System terminated.\\")\\n            return False\\n        \\n        print(f\\"Today ({today_str}) is a trading day. Proceeding...\\")\\n        return True\\n\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        print(f\\"Failed to check trading holiday: {e}. Proceeding anyway.\\")\\n        return True\\n\\ncheck_trading_day()\\n```\\n### 3. Key Concepts\\n* <mark>XKRX</mark>: This is the ISO code for the Korea Exchange. The US uses `XNYS` (New York Stock Exchange), `XNAS` (NASDAQ), etc.\\n* <mark>is_session()</mark>: Returns a `Boolean` value indicating whether a specific date is a trading day (open day). It includes both weekends and holidays.\\n### 4. More Tips\\nIf you want to get a list of all holidays within a specific period, you can automate scheduling using the `holidays_at` attribute or the `sessions_in_range` method."}')}}]);